   "evidence": "Lines 183-185, 299-300, 302-304 of the diff; `./mathlib/Mathlib/Order/Interval/Set/Defs.lean:80` \u2014 `@[simp, grind =, push, to_dual none] theorem mem_Icc : x \u2208 Icc a b \u2194 a \u2264 x \u2227 x \u2264 b := .rfl`. The repo's only other definitional `Iff.rfl` unfolding, `EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/LieAlgebra/SpecialUnitary.lean:114` (`mem_su_iff`), carries no `@[simp]`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Quarkonium/NRQCD/Scales.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `@[simp]` from `coulombicScaling_iff`, `weaklyCoupled_iff` and `stronglyCoupled_iff`; keep them as plain characterisation lemmas that a consumer invokes deliberately. If a simp-normal form for the Coulombic bound is wanted, annotate `coulombicScaling_iff_binding` instead, not the `Set.Icc` restatement.",
   "issue": "`@[simp] coulombicScaling_iff` (line 183-185), `@[simp] weaklyCoupled_iff` (299-300) and `@[simp] stronglyCoupled_iff` (302-304) are `Iff.rfl` unfoldings of the three Prop definitions the file introduces, so any downstream `simp` rewrites the named predicate away. For `CoulombicScaling` it is worse than unfolding: `Set.mem_Icc` is itself `@[simp]` in Mathlib, so `s.CoulombicScaling K` normalises all the way to `K\u207b\u00b9 \u2264 s.coulombRatio \u2227 s.coulombRatio \u2264 K`, after which `CoulombicScaling.one_le`, `CoulombicScaling.mono` and `coulombicScaling_iff_binding` no longer match the hypothesis; likewise `WeaklyCoupled.not_stronglyCoupled`, `WeaklyCoupled.hadronic_lt_momentum`, `StronglyCoupled.binding_lt_hadronic` and `StronglyCoupled.hadronic_lt_momentum` stop applying once `simp` has hit the hypothesis or goal. The roadmap's design is that these be carried explicitly as hypotheses through later layers ('records the regime as a hypothesis of every theorem that needs one'), which a default-simp-set unfolding defeats.",
   "line": 183
  }
 ],
